From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:22:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(ui): early stopping option in the training dialog

Additional options gain an "Early stopping" checkbox, off by default.
Ticking it shows "Patience (epochs)" (default 5, 1 to 1000) and an
optional "Minimum improvement" (empty means any drop counts). The job
payload carries early_stopping_patience, and early_stopping_min_delta
when one was entered, only while the box is ticked; otherwise neither
field is sent and the run trains for the full Max Epochs as before.

The model details show the early-stopping settings a model was trained
with.

openapi-spec.json/.d.ts are generated (gitignored); they were rebuilt
from this backend with main.app.openapi(), which is what the backend
serves at /api/openapi.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
